# Survey – generated by the "question-me" skill

## Round 1

```survey-json
{
  "round": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-11-22T18:20:16.000Z",
  "stage": "stage-1792362077711",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "In task history, every automatic resume currently says 'after server restart', even when the task was actually interrupted on the runner (about 100 of these in the data, with zero real server restarts). We plan to use two clear labels from now on: keep the server-restart wording only for real server restarts, and use a new 'after runner interrupt' wording (naming which runner and why) for runner cases. History rows already written stay as they are. Are you happy with that?",
      "options": [
        "Yes - use two separate labels (Recommended)",
        "No - keep the single 'server restart' label"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "The 'Tried N times' badge currently counts every automatic infrastructure resume as a try, which inflates it (the screenshot showed x6/x10/x11). We plan to stop counting these infra resumes as tries, so the badge shows only real attempts. How should infra resumes be shown?",
      "options": [
        "Show both, e.g. 'Tried 2 times, 4 infra resumes' (Recommended)",
        "Hide them, e.g. just 'Tried 2 times'",
        "Keep counting them as today (no change)"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "q1": {
      "selected": [
        "Yes - use two separate labels (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q2": {
      "selected": [
        "Show both, e.g. 'Tried 2 times, 4 infra resumes' (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    }
  }
}
```

